  "id": "Compound::DB01212 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "Ceftriaxone, a cephalosporin antibiotic, is linked to Slc22a11 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Ceftriaxone is included in the broader class of cephalosporins, which in turn bind to Slc22a11. This relationship is supported by multiple paths, all of which converge on the shared classification of Ceftriaxone and cephalosporins as part of the same family, followed by their binding to Slc22a11. The lowest common ancestors across these paths consistently point to the broader category of cephalosporins, reinforcing the hierarchical relationship between the antibiotic and the transporter. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where cephalosporins, through their interaction with Slc22a11, influence the transport of organic cations or anions, which is a key function of Slc22a11. This suggests that Ceftriaxone may exert its effects through a transporter-mediated pathway, with Slc22a11 playing a central role in the transport process.",
